	<h2 id="used">
		Used Car Tips V60
	</h2>
	<figure>
		<img src="~/images/models/V60/Used/01.jpg" class="img-thumbnail"/>
		<figcaption>
			A ship will come - but the steering lacks precision.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure>
		<img src="~/images/models/V60/Used/02.jpg" class="img-thumbnail"/>
		<figcaption>
			Mechanical engineering: The 3.2-litre turbodiesel is rock solid, but shakes the car
			vigorously on start-up.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure>
		<img src="~/images/models/V60/Used/03.jpg" class="img-thumbnail"/>
		<figcaption>
			Caution is advised at welded seams and cut edges.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure>
		<img src="~/images/models/V60/Used/04.jpg" class="img-thumbnail"/>
		<figcaption>
			Switch and command: The cockpit controls are simple throughout; only for
			handling the four-wheel drive is a look at the owner's manual recommended.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure>
		<img src="~/images/models/V60/Used/05.jpg" class="img-thumbnail"/>
		<figcaption>
			Family friend: as a five-door with up to seven seats.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure>
		<img src="~/images/models/V60/Used/06.jpg" class="img-thumbnail"/>
		<figcaption>
			The tie rod and anti-roll bar linkage tend to develop excessive play, which causes noises
			and unsettles the MOT inspector.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure>
		<img src="~/images/models/V60/Used/07.jpg" class="img-thumbnail"/>
		<figcaption>
			The electrics are insufficiently protected against water and correspondingly failure-prone.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure>
		<img src="~/images/models/V60/Used/08.jpg" class="img-thumbnail" />
		<figcaption>
			The vacuum actuation for the gearbox and differential locks is unreliable.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>
